message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. To cite the associated research paper, use the
  preferred-citation entry.

type: software
title: >-
  CIPA: A Multi-Domain Statistical Framework for Characterizing
  Imbalanced Datasets and Computing a Difficulty Score
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-05-05"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/luisgarciarodriguez-research/cipa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/luisgarciarodriguez-research/cipa"

abstract: >-
  CIPA (Characterization, Indexing, Profiling, Action) is a domain-agnostic
  Python framework that characterizes imbalanced binary classification datasets
  along seven non-redundant complexity dimensions (D1-D7) and aggregates them
  into a normalized Difficulty Score (DS) in [0, 1]. It produces a structural
  fingerprint (Complexity Signature I-V) and actionable recommendations for
  evaluation metric selection, preprocessing strategy, model family, and
  validation protocol — all without training any model. Validated across 13
  publicly available datasets from five domains, DS achieves Spearman
  rho = -0.71 against reference AUC-PR values, significantly outperforming
  the imbalance ratio alone (Wilcoxon p = 0.040).

keywords:
  - imbalanced learning
  - data complexity measures
  - classification difficulty
  - difficulty score
  - meta-learning
  - preprocessing selection
  - class overlap
  - instance hardness
  - sub-concept fragmentation

